  "title": "World&#39;s Fastest Meatballs",
  "description": "This recipe for the world&#39;s fastest meatballs is made with beef and veal. Simmer the meatballs in tomato sauce for a spaghetti and meatball dinner.",
  "authors": [
    "John Mitzewich"
  ],
  "date_published": "2012-05-29T17:40:28-04:00",
  "date_modified": "2025-02-12T10:27:44-05:00",
  "prep_time": "PT30M",
  "cook_time": "PT30M",
  "total_time": "PT60M",
  "yield": [
    "6",
    "48 meatballs"
  ],
  "categories": [
    "Dinner"
  ],
  "cuisines": [
    "Italian Inspired"
  ],
  "regions": [
    "Italian Inspired"
  ],
  "breadcrumbs": [],
  "keywords": [],
  "ingredients": [
    "6 cups prepared tomato sauce",
    "0.5 cup dry bread crumbs",
    "0.25 cup milk",
    "1 large egg",
    "2 teaspoons Italian herb seasoning",
    "2 teaspoons olive oil",
    "0.5 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "0.25 teaspoon red pepper flakes",
    "1 pound ground beef",
    "1 pound ground veal",
    "1.5 teaspoons salt",
    "0.5 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper",
    "0.25 teaspoon ground white pepper",
    "0.33333334326744 cup finely grated Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Pour tomato sauce into a large stockpot; bring to a simmer over medium heat. Reduce heat to low; keep sauce warm while preparing meatballs.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Set an oven rack about 6 inches from the heat source and preheat the oven's broiler. Line a baking sheet with aluminum foil; brush lightly with oil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine bread crumbs, milk, egg, Italian herb seasoning, olive oil, garlic powder, and red pepper flakes in a small bowl until forms a thick slurry; set aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine beef and veal in a large bowl; season with salt, black pepper, and white pepper. Sprinkle with Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese. Add slurry mixture; mix until combined.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Scoop meat mixture using a small ice cream scooper into about 48 meatballs; place on the prepared baking sheet.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook under the preheated broiler until browned, 4 to 5 minutes; flip meatballs. Broil until no longer pink in centers and browned on both sides, 3 to 4 minutes more.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer meatballs to the simmering tomato sauce. Increase heat to medium; cook for 5 to 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Am-vb5VLfGrzYxX6MFBPIiChNgY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/860570-f25d70d0a849459fa166a60b4d9f4723.jpg"
      ],
